1
00:00:14,460 --> 00:00:25,420
Melody Cle, catching the wind of the season,
a shining, greatest debut

2
00:00:27,120 --> 00:00:37,460
Lightly leaping past these hectic times,
diving into the city, playing the hero

3
00:00:37,460 --> 00:00:39,720
I wanna die with you for the night

4
00:00:39,720 --> 00:00:49,120
Wearing only the latest trends,
my bare face suits me best, so

5
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:51,000
Let it bleed!

6
00:00:51,940 --> 00:00:58,240
Everybody can do it,
the dreams we set off chasing never stop

7
00:00:58,240 --> 00:01:03,560
Let's go out and face tomorrow's regrets,
Let it wild!

8
00:01:03,560 --> 00:01:10,820
Everybody can, a little stepping
outside the lines doesn't hurt

9
00:01:10,820 --> 00:01:18,120
Holding onto our restless curiosity,
we flew strong and high

10
00:01:28,860 --> 00:01:31,580
Run, Honda, for love

11
00:01:41,900 --> 00:01:44,900
Move, move! Don't run in the middle of the virtual road,
you idiot!

12
00:01:52,840 --> 00:01:55,500
Hey Nakagawa, aren't you getting hungry?

13
00:01:56,040 --> 00:01:58,700
How about we have liver and leek
stir-fry and a gyoza set meal today?

14
00:01:58,700 --> 00:02:00,540
Chinese food? That sounds good.

15
00:02:03,880 --> 00:02:12,440
Uoooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooh!

16
00:02:12,780 --> 00:02:14,220
Honda! That was dangerous!

17
00:02:14,980 --> 00:02:17,020
Don't get so angry, Mr. Ryotsu.

18
00:02:18,840 --> 00:02:21,040
Anyway, I'm going to buy a bento now.

19
00:02:21,360 --> 00:02:22,540
I'll go buy one for you too.

20
00:02:22,540 --> 00:02:23,900
Don't bother, I'm ordering delivery today.

21
00:02:24,500 --> 00:02:26,380
Even if I say I'm treating you?

22
00:02:28,460 --> 00:02:31,400
Honda-kun, why didn't you say that earlier?

23
00:02:32,580 --> 00:02:34,820
I'll have the premium
tenderloin cutlet set meal.

24
00:02:34,820 --> 00:02:36,920
Maybe I'll add some pork miso soup too,
for once.

25
00:02:37,720 --> 00:02:39,980
Geez, what a spry old geezer.

26
00:02:40,520 --> 00:02:41,320
Nakagawa, what about you?

27
00:02:42,440 --> 00:02:49,380
Are you sure? Since I'm at it... this is Senior Nakagawa's treat,
so get something cheap. Then, chicken karaage bento.

28
00:02:49,380 --> 00:02:50,140
Same.

29
00:02:50,140 --> 00:02:58,440
Okay then, Senior Nakagawa, we're off!

30
00:02:58,880 --> 00:03:03,720
Someone who changes personality that drastically is rare,
isn't it?

31
00:03:05,720 --> 00:03:06,080
Thank you very much.

32
00:03:11,180 --> 00:03:11,580
Hello.

33
00:03:13,100 --> 00:03:15,780
Welcome! Bento again today?

34
00:03:15,780 --> 00:03:19,640
Yes, because the bento here
is absolutely delicious.

35
00:03:19,640 --> 00:03:22,980
Thank you! What will it be today?

36
00:03:24,040 --> 00:03:27,200
The special fillet cutlet bento
and the karaage bento, please.

37
00:03:27,600 --> 00:03:30,780
I'll have the nori bento.
And for the rest, two karaage each, please.

38
00:03:31,640 --> 00:03:37,040
So that's two each of the special fillet cutlet bento,
the karaage bento, and the nori bento, right?

39
00:03:37,560 --> 00:03:39,400
I made a mistake.

40
00:03:41,740 --> 00:03:42,960
Ahaha.

41
00:03:43,560 --> 00:03:46,180
No, that's fine. And miso soup too.

42
00:03:46,180 --> 00:03:48,160
Six miso soups, right?

43
00:03:48,160 --> 00:03:49,360
Yes.

44
00:03:49,880 --> 00:03:54,320
Manager, two each of special fillet,
karaage, nori bento, and miso soup coming up.

45
00:03:54,320 --> 00:03:54,920
Here you go.

46
00:03:56,360 --> 00:03:58,680
Here are two makunouchi. Thanks for waiting.

47
00:04:06,740 --> 00:04:09,020
Thanks for paying for us too,
sorry about that.

48
00:04:09,480 --> 00:04:12,180
Not at all, we're always in your debt.

49
00:04:12,180 --> 00:04:14,200
That's the kind of attitude that matters.

50
00:04:14,960 --> 00:04:17,680
Unlike some people I could mention.

51
00:04:17,680 --> 00:04:19,140
The Chief says so too.

52
00:04:19,140 --> 00:04:20,540
Some people I could mention.

53
00:04:20,540 --> 00:04:22,520
I mean you, you!

54
00:04:23,960 --> 00:04:26,580
Isn't the rice here a little dry?

55
00:04:26,780 --> 00:04:27,780
Now that you mention it, it is.

56
00:04:28,440 --> 00:04:29,900
No, that's not true at all.

57
00:04:30,780 --> 00:04:32,380
They use Koshihikari rice here, after all.

58
00:04:32,380 --> 00:04:33,300
Mm.

59
00:04:33,300 --> 00:04:36,220
The pickles are a little salty, too.

60
00:04:36,220 --> 00:04:38,340
This much is just right.

61
00:04:38,860 --> 00:04:40,620
This shop's bento is the best.

62
00:04:40,620 --> 00:04:43,500
After all, it's made with love.

63
00:04:43,500 --> 00:04:44,220
I figured it out.

64
00:04:45,300 --> 00:04:47,760
You went and deliberately miscounted the bentos,
didn't you?

65
00:04:47,760 --> 00:04:51,160
Are you getting paid to be
this bento shop's promoter?

66
00:04:51,940 --> 00:04:53,320
N-no, it's not like that.

67
00:04:53,320 --> 00:04:54,380
Got it.

68
00:04:55,060 --> 00:04:55,806
Honda,

69
00:04:55,856 --> 00:04:59,200
you have a thing for the girl at that bento shop,
don't you?

70
00:05:01,920 --> 00:05:03,680
Wh-what? No, that's not...

71
00:05:03,680 --> 00:05:07,220
I see. That shop girl is cute, isn't she?

72
00:05:07,220 --> 00:05:09,840
How did you figure that out?

73
00:05:09,840 --> 00:05:13,020
Anyone could tell from that
red-light face of yours!

74
00:05:13,020 --> 00:05:14,320
You're so naive.

75
00:05:14,320 --> 00:05:17,040
So what's the shop girl's name?

76
00:05:18,320 --> 00:05:20,420
Her name's Megumi Hoshino.

77
00:05:21,020 --> 00:05:24,600
Thanks, Honda. Now give up on that girl.

78
00:05:24,600 --> 00:05:26,880
Wh-why? Why would you say that, senpai?

79
00:05:27,240 --> 00:05:29,581
Ryo-chan, are you even my friend?

80
00:05:29,631 --> 00:05:31,320
You should help him out.

81
00:05:31,580 --> 00:05:32,827
Reiko, you see,

82
00:05:32,877 --> 00:05:36,120
do you have any idea how many
times this guy has been dumped?

83
00:05:36,760 --> 00:05:39,400
Not once or twice. A hundred times.

84
00:05:39,700 --> 00:05:41,760
To be precise, it's a hundred and one times.

85
00:05:41,980 --> 00:05:42,560
That many?

86
00:05:42,860 --> 00:05:46,480
Every time, I'm dragged along to drown his sorrows.
Try seeing it from my side.

87
00:05:47,200 --> 00:05:47,840
But...

88
00:05:47,840 --> 00:05:49,480
Reiko-kun, I'd stop if I were you.

89
00:05:49,900 --> 00:05:52,120
Ryotsu was born with no talent for romance,

90
00:05:52,170 --> 00:05:54,560
so there's no way he can play Cupid.

91
00:05:57,040 --> 00:05:58,520
I can't let that slide.

92
00:06:00,280 --> 00:06:01,100
*Splash!*

93
00:06:01,800 --> 00:06:02,120
What?

94
00:06:03,000 --> 00:06:07,900
It's rude to call me the handsome
middle-aged man who kills women.

95
00:06:08,360 --> 00:06:10,720
What handsome middle-aged
man who kills women?

96
00:06:11,060 --> 00:06:12,800
Keep your jokes to your eyebrows.

97
00:06:13,400 --> 00:06:13,840
Well then,

98
00:06:15,140 --> 00:06:19,200
right, now I'll get that girl
and Honda together no matter what.

99
00:06:19,200 --> 00:06:20,640
Really, senpai?

100
00:06:21,580 --> 00:06:24,100
Leave it to me and rest easy,
like you're on a big tall tale.

101
00:06:24,100 --> 00:06:25,320
You mean "big ship," right?

102
00:06:26,880 --> 00:06:30,200
Anyway! I'll definitely get
you and Megumi-chan together!

103
00:06:30,880 --> 00:06:32,240
I'm counting on you, senpai!

104
00:06:58,940 --> 00:07:00,280
How did it go, senior?

105
00:07:00,960 --> 00:07:03,780
There's a hopeless guy she likes.

106
00:07:05,320 --> 00:07:05,720
No way.

107
00:07:12,760 --> 00:07:15,540
What kind of guy is this man she likes?

108
00:07:16,700 --> 00:07:20,460
Apparently she admires the White Plum
officer who passes here at nine every morning.

109
00:07:20,960 --> 00:07:21,840
Well, thanks a lot.

110
00:07:21,840 --> 00:07:23,920
Give up on Megumi already.

111
00:07:25,260 --> 00:07:28,120
But I'm a White Plum member too!

112
00:07:30,260 --> 00:07:33,600
I pass in front of the shop
at nine every morning too!

113
00:07:36,060 --> 00:07:37,180
What did you just say?

114
00:07:39,460 --> 00:07:42,280
I said I pass in front of the
shop at nine every morning too.

115
00:07:43,740 --> 00:07:45,080
Come here, Honda.

116
00:07:47,840 --> 00:07:48,620
Hey, miss, excuse me for a sec.

117
00:07:48,620 --> 00:07:49,320
Yes?

118
00:07:49,960 --> 00:07:53,200
Isn't this the Hakubai
guy you mentioned earlier?

119
00:07:53,920 --> 00:07:54,120
See!

120
00:07:55,780 --> 00:07:57,440
The one who always comes in to buy

121
00:07:57,440 --> 00:07:59,260
H-hello there.

122
00:07:59,680 --> 00:08:01,100
Well? Doesn't he look like him?

123
00:08:01,160 --> 00:08:04,520
No way, he doesn't look alike at all.

124
00:08:07,640 --> 00:08:08,820
Sorry.

125
00:08:09,680 --> 00:08:13,860
He's a bit similar in being slim,
but his face is much more chiseled.

126
00:08:13,860 --> 00:08:16,940
He always has his sleeves rolled up
and his scarf flapping in the wind.

127
00:08:16,940 --> 00:08:19,400
He's really manly and cool, you know.

128
00:08:20,660 --> 00:08:22,200
Well, it's obviously me.

129
00:08:23,920 --> 00:08:24,460
Ask me!

130
00:08:24,560 --> 00:08:25,100
Senior!

131
00:08:28,620 --> 00:08:30,980
But the face looks different after all...

132
00:08:30,980 --> 00:08:32,878
I know it's hard to believe,

133
00:08:32,928 --> 00:08:37,520
but when this Honda gets on a bike,
his face and personality completely change!

134
00:08:38,000 --> 00:08:39,560
So your name is Honda?

135
00:08:39,940 --> 00:08:41,050
This Honda here,

136
00:08:41,100 --> 00:08:44,580
is the top rider among all
the active Hakubai officers!

137
00:08:45,800 --> 00:08:49,005
That's right!
If it's Honda, a fellow Hakubai officer,

138
00:08:49,055 --> 00:08:52,620
you'd know who passes in front
of this shop every morning, right?

139
00:08:53,920 --> 00:08:54,680
No, not that.

140
00:08:54,680 --> 00:08:57,900
Yes, it's fine. Leave it to me.

141
00:08:59,440 --> 00:09:02,820
Then, Honda-san, once you find
out his name, let me know, okay?

142
00:09:03,220 --> 00:09:03,580
Yeah.

143
00:09:07,500 --> 00:09:10,020
Geez, you went and made
an unnecessary promise.

144
00:09:10,020 --> 00:09:11,120
Sorry.

145
00:09:11,720 --> 00:09:13,800
I see, things have gotten complicated.

146
00:09:13,800 --> 00:09:16,999
Megumi-san likes Honda
when he's riding his bike,

147
00:09:17,049 --> 00:09:19,080
so the current Honda won't do?

148
00:09:22,640 --> 00:09:26,340
Well then, there's only one way left.
What should I do?

149
00:09:26,940 --> 00:09:30,820
From now on, you keep riding
that bike in front of Megumi-chan.

150
00:09:32,700 --> 00:09:38,780
That's impossible, impossible, I know, but if you ask
her out while still on the bike, she'll definitely say yes.

151
00:09:38,780 --> 00:09:42,920
No doubt about it. Well, maybe so, but...

152
00:09:42,920 --> 00:09:49,140
Between men and women, the first impression is what counts.
Nail it right there, and everything else will take care of itself.

153
00:09:50,640 --> 00:09:52,140
Is that how it works?

154
00:09:52,640 --> 00:09:56,020
The ladies' killer, a nice middle-aged man,
says so, so there's no doubt.

155
00:09:58,660 --> 00:09:59,520
I'll do it.

156
00:09:59,520 --> 00:10:00,400
Honda-san.

157
00:10:00,400 --> 00:10:02,740
I really like her.

158
00:10:02,740 --> 00:10:05,000
If I could go on a date
with someone that lovely,

159
00:10:05,000 --> 00:10:07,060
I wouldn't care what happened after that.

160
00:10:08,100 --> 00:10:09,380
Alright, it's settled.

161
00:10:09,380 --> 00:10:11,260
Now all that's left is to go for it.

162
00:10:11,260 --> 00:10:12,540
Yes, senior.

163
00:10:22,640 --> 00:10:23,540
Aaaaah!

164
00:10:27,240 --> 00:10:30,840
So Honda-san told you Well, yeah.

165
00:10:30,840 --> 00:10:37,420
Sorry. Nice to meet you, I'm Megumi Hoshino.
What's your name?

166
00:10:38,180 --> 00:10:45,000
I'm Honda. You're Honda-san too?
No, I'm Suzuki, the one next to Honda.

167
00:10:45,380 --> 00:10:46,400
Suzuki-san?

168
00:10:47,180 --> 00:10:49,500
I've got a rule about not giving
women rides on my bike, but...

169
00:10:49,980 --> 00:10:53,960
How about it? Trust your life to me
and feel the wind together with me?

170
00:10:58,100 --> 00:10:59,260
I'd love to!

171
00:10:59,680 --> 00:11:02,760
Then I'll come pick you up
right here Sunday morning at nine.

172
00:11:02,760 --> 00:11:03,440
Yes.

173
00:11:04,260 --> 00:11:04,800
See ya.

174
00:11:14,180 --> 00:11:15,840
Looks like the prize money's mine, then.

175
00:11:19,700 --> 00:11:20,840
Ryo-san, you're the man!

176
00:11:20,840 --> 00:11:22,920
I did it!

177
00:11:23,380 --> 00:11:24,780
I've got a date on Sunday!

178
00:11:24,780 --> 00:11:26,620
Oh yeah? Nice work!

179
00:11:27,040 --> 00:11:31,040
Listen, during the date,
don't you dare get off the bike, got it?

180
00:11:31,640 --> 00:11:32,000
Yes.

181
00:11:45,060 --> 00:11:45,840
Mr. Suzuki

182
00:11:47,620 --> 00:11:48,540
Mr. Suzuki

183
00:11:49,340 --> 00:11:50,100
Whoa, what is it?

184
00:11:50,100 --> 00:11:54,620
I had no idea the wind could feel this good.

185
00:11:54,620 --> 00:11:56,840
Well, I'm glad to hear it.

186
00:11:58,660 --> 00:12:00,280
I was Suzuki, wasn't I?

187
00:12:00,280 --> 00:12:00,360
You're...

188
00:12:02,160 --> 00:12:03,680
You're...

189
00:12:08,320 --> 00:12:10,080
Don't go there, Ryo!

190
00:12:15,760 --> 00:12:18,020
Don't go cruising around
with some girl on your bike!

191
00:12:20,000 --> 00:12:22,560
Who do you think you're talking to?!

192
00:12:23,380 --> 00:12:24,360
H-Honda-san!

193
00:12:25,960 --> 00:12:28,540
I'm not Honda!
I'm the top man in this outfit!

194
00:12:32,880 --> 00:12:34,572
I-I'm really sorry.

195
00:12:34,622 --> 00:12:37,360
I never imagined you were Mr. Honda,
so I...

196
00:12:38,360 --> 00:12:39,420
It's Suzuki, you idiot!

197
00:12:39,860 --> 00:12:41,080
Please forgive me, Mr. Suzuki!

198
00:12:41,780 --> 00:12:43,240
Please forgive me, Mr. Suzuki!

199
00:12:43,600 --> 00:12:44,500
Just understand that.

200
00:12:45,380 --> 00:12:47,260
Well, I'll let it go for today,

201
00:12:47,800 --> 00:12:50,140
but if you pull a stunt like that again,
you'll answer to me!

202
00:12:50,700 --> 00:12:50,980
Yes, sir!

203
00:12:52,360 --> 00:12:52,840
Are you all right?

204
00:12:53,220 --> 00:12:57,180
Y-yes, as long as Mr. Suzuki is with me,
I'm not scared at all.

205
00:12:58,540 --> 00:13:00,020
Okay, hold on tight.

206
00:13:00,820 --> 00:13:01,100
Yes!

207
00:13:09,860 --> 00:13:13,620
That's strange, it really was Honda, though.

208
00:13:32,940 --> 00:13:36,020
Suzuki, you really are manly and strong.

209
00:13:36,020 --> 00:13:38,320
Hey, I'm so moved.

210
00:13:38,880 --> 00:13:39,520
You idiot.

211
00:13:40,600 --> 00:13:41,640
Want to watch a movie or something?

212
00:13:41,740 --> 00:13:42,140
Yes.

213
00:13:51,500 --> 00:13:52,820
There's an empty seat, though.

214
00:13:52,820 --> 00:13:55,980
I always watch it like this,
so don't mind me.

215
00:13:56,620 --> 00:13:58,020
You're a strange one, aren't you.

216
00:14:43,840 --> 00:14:49,020
Good work today.

217
00:14:50,580 --> 00:14:52,560
You're the best partner there is, after all.

218
00:14:52,560 --> 00:14:55,320
My bike and I are one.

219
00:14:58,760 --> 00:15:00,480
The best partner

220
00:15:09,140 --> 00:15:10,140
What's wrong?

221
00:15:11,460 --> 00:15:15,880
Actually, the guy I've been
dating goes to America today.

222
00:15:17,040 --> 00:15:18,360
So you had a boyfriend.

223
00:15:20,060 --> 00:15:21,460
Transferred to America?

224
00:15:24,840 --> 00:15:28,400
M-Megumi, c-come to America with me...

225
00:15:29,900 --> 00:15:32,080
No, never mind.

226
00:15:32,760 --> 00:15:35,940
Ha two years will fly by.
We'll see each other again, right?

227
00:15:39,200 --> 00:15:40,360
That's all I had to say.

228
00:15:40,600 --> 00:15:40,960
What?

229
00:15:41,880 --> 00:15:45,078
Go wherever you like,
America or anywhere else.

230
00:15:45,128 --> 00:15:45,940
Goodbye.

231
00:15:46,240 --> 00:15:47,680
M-Megumi!

232
00:15:53,700 --> 00:15:54,640
It's fine, really.

233
00:15:56,160 --> 00:15:57,260
It's already over.

234
00:15:57,260 --> 00:15:58,960
A wishy-washy guy like that

235
00:15:58,960 --> 00:16:00,640
I'm glad to be rid of him.

236
00:16:03,700 --> 00:16:07,220
A man really has to be manly like Suzuki.

237
00:16:08,860 --> 00:16:09,620
I see.

238
00:16:11,900 --> 00:16:12,960
Shall we head back soon?

239
00:16:13,640 --> 00:16:14,020
Yes.

240
00:16:17,660 --> 00:16:18,020
Yes.

241
00:16:18,820 --> 00:16:20,300
Yes, welcome!

242
00:16:25,760 --> 00:16:27,360
What's wrong?

243
00:16:27,840 --> 00:16:29,520
Just wait here a moment.

244
00:16:35,480 --> 00:16:36,940
Alright, it's done!

245
00:16:36,940 --> 00:16:39,060
I'm gonna leak!

246
00:16:41,500 --> 00:16:43,340
How did the data turn out?

247
00:16:44,300 --> 00:16:45,869
Just as you told me in the first half,

248
00:16:45,919 --> 00:16:49,320
I kept riding my motorbike the whole time,
so it's perfect.

249
00:16:49,320 --> 00:16:50,700
I see, you know what they say,
on the contrary

250
00:17:09,180 --> 00:17:10,180
Megumi-san

251
00:17:11,220 --> 00:17:12,240
Yamamoto-san

252
00:17:14,700 --> 00:17:17,140
Senpai,
please don't get in the way this time.

253
00:17:17,660 --> 00:17:20,180
Who do you think made this date happen?

254
00:17:27,900 --> 00:17:29,660
Who's that man?

255
00:17:31,620 --> 00:17:32,273
Actually, today,

256
00:17:32,323 --> 00:17:35,840
the guy I've been dating for a
long time is going off to America.

257
00:17:40,280 --> 00:17:43,060
Hey, Honda, explain. Who is he?

258
00:17:44,340 --> 00:17:46,800
Hey, hey, wait, you son of a bitch!

259
00:17:48,380 --> 00:17:51,820
I just had to tell you how
I feel before she leaves,

260
00:17:52,280 --> 00:17:52,440
What?

261
00:17:54,620 --> 00:17:56,378
M-Megumi-san, I... I

262
00:17:56,428 --> 00:17:58,960
I love you! I want to marry you!

263
00:18:02,260 --> 00:18:05,960
I got you a plane ticket too.
I want you to come with me, if possible.

264
00:18:08,980 --> 00:18:10,160
You can't just say that all of a sudden!

265
00:18:10,400 --> 00:18:13,340
Right, of course that's impossible,
isn't it.

266
00:18:14,360 --> 00:18:16,180
That's always how it goes for me

267
00:18:19,140 --> 00:18:20,220
Well, take care.

268
00:18:38,460 --> 00:18:39,440
You're late.

269
00:18:39,440 --> 00:18:40,800
Do you have your passport?

270
00:18:41,560 --> 00:18:42,900
I'm asking if you have it.

271
00:18:46,320 --> 00:18:47,927
If we stop by your place,

272
00:18:47,977 --> 00:18:50,840
let's take a touring trip
all the way to Narita next.

273
00:18:51,600 --> 00:18:56,840
Damn it! You stray dog!
Next time I see you, I'll arrest you!

274
00:18:58,700 --> 00:18:59,500
Honda!

275
00:19:00,540 --> 00:19:01,920
Why is Honda here?

276
00:19:04,140 --> 00:19:06,540
You like her, don't you? That guy Yamamodo?

277
00:19:10,500 --> 00:19:12,600
Manliness isn't just about how you look.

278
00:19:13,020 --> 00:19:15,680
Keeping devotion to the woman you love,
single-mindedly,

279
00:19:15,680 --> 00:19:17,700
I think that's manly.

280
00:19:18,540 --> 00:19:19,320
Suzuki-san.

281
00:19:25,200 --> 00:19:28,180
Of all places, we had to get stuck here.

282
00:19:31,460 --> 00:19:34,000
What time does the plane leave?

283
00:19:34,000 --> 00:19:35,180
Seven o'clock.

284
00:19:38,180 --> 00:19:40,800
Damn it, at this rate we won't make it.

285
00:19:42,740 --> 00:19:44,120
Hold on tight.

286
00:20:13,740 --> 00:20:15,000
Thanks, everyone.

287
00:20:15,000 --> 00:20:17,500
Hey, don't look so glum.

288
00:20:17,500 --> 00:20:21,100
Going to Los Angeles means you're on the fast track to promotion,
after all.

289
00:20:28,400 --> 00:20:29,460
Well, I'm off then.

290
00:20:29,460 --> 00:20:30,880
Do your best over there.

291
00:20:30,880 --> 00:20:31,500
Yeah.

292
00:20:37,820 --> 00:20:38,520
Take care of yourself.

293
00:20:38,520 --> 00:20:40,060
Give us a call every now and then.

294
00:20:40,580 --> 00:20:41,360
Good luck.

295
00:21:02,220 --> 00:21:03,460
M-Megumi-san...

296
00:21:10,720 --> 00:21:11,700
Go on, go to her.

297
00:21:24,680 --> 00:21:25,460
Together

298
00:21:26,900 --> 00:21:28,740
I've decided to go with him.

299
00:21:30,080 --> 00:21:31,680
Please take me with you too.

300
00:21:34,700 --> 00:21:35,760
Megumi-san

301
00:21:37,740 --> 00:21:39,360
What are you still doing here?

302
00:21:39,960 --> 00:21:41,680
Hurry, or you'll miss the flight!

303
00:21:43,400 --> 00:21:44,120
Suzuki-san

304
00:21:44,480 --> 00:21:45,900
I don't know how to thank you.

305
00:21:45,900 --> 00:21:47,560
Never mind about me.

306
00:21:47,560 --> 00:21:48,500
Just go.

307
00:21:48,880 --> 00:21:49,240
Yes.

308
00:21:50,160 --> 00:21:50,520
Thank you so much.

309
00:22:11,740 --> 00:22:14,240
Honda-san, so it was you.

310
00:22:26,200 --> 00:22:27,760
Thank you, Honda-san.

311
00:22:35,080 --> 00:22:35,600
Thank you.

312
00:22:35,600 --> 00:22:37,200
Honda-san.

313
00:22:41,000 --> 00:22:42,280
Goodbye.

314
00:22:42,280 --> 00:22:43,360
Megumi-san.

315
00:22:52,320 --> 00:22:54,580
She was such a good girl, though.

316
00:22:54,580 --> 00:22:56,820
My 102nd love, too...

317
00:22:58,740 --> 00:23:03,780
Oh well, and on top of that, I'll be down for half a year.
What else can I do?

318
00:23:05,540 --> 00:23:12,800
Still, playing Cupid for the woman you love...
you're too nice for your own good, or just plain stupid.

319
00:23:12,800 --> 00:23:20,020
You're just like Ryo-san when he was young.
Like you, he'd get dead drunk here every time he was dumped.

320
00:23:20,020 --> 00:23:20,760
What about Ryo-san?

321
00:23:20,800 --> 00:23:22,700
Old man, don't say unnecessary things.

322
00:23:22,700 --> 00:23:24,280
What's the harm in it?

323
00:23:24,660 --> 00:23:28,120
Hey, Honda, 102 heartbreaks?
That's nothing, nothing at all!

324
00:23:28,120 --> 00:23:31,000
Ryo-san's been over 300!

325
00:23:31,000 --> 00:23:32,220
Really?

326
00:23:32,500 --> 00:23:35,260
Th-that's actually cheering me up a little.

327
00:23:35,920 --> 00:23:37,860
Senpai, let's keep drinking!

328
00:23:38,500 --> 00:23:38,913
But,

329
00:23:38,963 --> 00:23:43,440
at this rate, we'll be hungover and
get chewed out by the Chief again!

330
00:23:43,960 --> 00:23:45,480
Isn't that just the usual?

331
00:23:45,940 --> 00:23:46,440
What?

332
00:23:46,440 --> 00:23:46,680
Yeah, yeah!

333
00:23:46,840 --> 00:23:48,960
Well, if that's how it is, to hell with it!

334
00:23:49,100 --> 00:23:50,780
We're drinking every last
drop of booze in this place!

335
00:23:51,740 --> 00:23:52,680
Yes! Senpai!

336
00:24:06,300 --> 00:24:08,540
Hello! What a fine spread you've ordered...

337
00:24:08,540 --> 00:24:11,180
You're only serving us tea? Chief!

338
00:24:11,680 --> 00:24:15,040
Your adorable subordinates have come all the way out to this mountain hideaway,
after all.

339
00:24:17,120 --> 00:24:20,940
Next time, the Ohara family treasure,
so be sure to show it.

340
00:24:46,440 --> 00:24:48,080
And let's go on living,

341
00:24:50,240 --> 00:24:57,960
even if today is rainy,

342
00:24:59,460 --> 00:25:03,480
tomorrow will be sunny.

343
00:25:04,300 --> 00:25:08,620
Bye-bye, let's wave goodbye,

344
00:25:08,620 --> 00:25:13,860
unpleasant things, farewell.

345
00:25:13,860 --> 00:25:21,480
Oh yeah, let's try living as we like.

346
00:25:21,480 --> 00:25:23,940
Good things will come.

347
00:25:23,940 --> 00:25:30,280
Outside the door, the sun is calling you.

348
00:25:43,860 --> 00:25:44,000
Thanks for watching.

